  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/tre100.html",
  "prefLabel": "Tre 102.03 Treasury Organization",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Tre 102.03 Treasury Organization. The treasury shall be organized as follows:\n\n(a) The office of investment and debt management, which shall:\n\n(1) Be under the direction of the chief deputy treasurer acting as the executive director of the office; and\n\n(2) Manage the state's investments, debt, cash flow and any other functions assigned by the treasurer.\n\n(b) The program of management and disbursements, established by the treasurer which shall:\n\n(1) Be under the direction of an assistant treasurer managing the programs; and\n\n(2) Administer state disbursements, account reconciliation, human resources, budgeting, and any other duties assigned by the treasurer.\n\n(c) The management information systems program, established by the treasurer, which shall:\n\n(1) Be under the direction of an information technology manager acting as the manager of the program; and\n\n(2) Manage systems development, maintenance, technical support and any other duties assigned by the treasurer.\n\n(d) The abandoned property division, established by the treasurer, which shall:\n\n(1) Be under the direction of the director of the abandoned property division; and\n\n(2) Manage the abandoned property program and any other duties assigned by the treasurer.\n\nSource. #7588, eff 11-7-01; ss by #9574, eff 10-22-09",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/tre100.html"
